  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Fold a short human DNA/RNA sequence with ViennaRNA, score its hairpins with a logistic-regression classifier, and show a ranked, explainable shortlist of pre-miRNA-like candidates with structure, feature sensitivity, matches to curated references and Rfam decoys, and machinery/literature evidence. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
